%description:

Tcp.maxReordering:invalid -- a value below dupthresh stops the run with an error.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "at least dupthresh".

The classes: linux (300, the default, the value of Linux tcp_max_reordering), caps (a value
below the reordering of the path), invalid (below dupthresh). The code:
Rfc6675Recovery::checkSackReordering() limits the degree to the value;
TcpConnection::configureStateVariables() checks it.

Host under test: host1. Observation: the error, and the exit code of the run.

%# parameter: Tcp.maxReordering
%# class: invalid
%# value: 2
%# key: *.host1.tcp.maxReordering
%# expected-result: PASS

%activity:
EV << "TcpMaxReorderingInvalid compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.maxReordering = 2    # the parameter under test
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%exitcode: 1

%contains-regex: stderr
maxReordering must be at least dupthresh \(3\), but it is 2
